{"availability":"available","full":"dguywhoknows/debate-simulator","name":"debate-simulator","description":"Two AI personas debate any motion in parliamentary format while an AI adjudicator scores the clash.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T03:29:14Z","updated":"2026-10-10T03:49:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/debate-simulator/","topics":["debate","github-pages","javascript","llm","text-analysis"],"demo":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/debate-simulator/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.575Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.575Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.575Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.575Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Two AI personas debate any motion in parliamentary format while an AI adjudicator scores the clash.","Pick a motion, give each side a persona and a speaking style, and watch a full debate unfold: openings, rebuttal rounds and closings, streamed token by token. Every speaker sees the full transcript, so rebuttals respond to what was actually said. A separate judge model then scores both sides against a rubric and maps the key clashes. Meanwhile the app runs its own text analysis on each side's speeches."],"features":["Configurable personas, style (formal / spicy / Socratic / ELI12) and number of rebuttal rounds","Live streaming speeches with full-transcript context for real rebuttals","AI judge returns structured JSON: rubric scores, clash map, margin, advice","SVG radar chart comparing both sides on logic, evidence, rebuttal and delivery","Local analytics: Flesch readability, evidence markers, hedge words, direct call-outs"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/debate-simulator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"83906b875e773d549b1dd83929d1e6989dc4789026cf47de0f81c9d880b495d6","extractedAt":"20